--- body ---
## Context

Implement the selected report-only design from `docs/discussions/2026-10-14-1095-design.md`: scan likely temporary locations, attribute candidate paths to local runtime histories where evidence exists, and report at roar/lair. The session-start healthcheck warns when `/tmp` or `/home` is low on space. This is a child of tracker 1095; it must not delete candidate content.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/session_scratch.py` and healthcheck implementation -- existing scanning and startup check
- `skills/roar/SKILL.md`, `skills/lair/SKILL.md` -- lifecycle invocation points
- `tests/` -- fixture-based tests for all supported readers and report scopes
- `docs/discussions/2026-10-14-1095-design.md` -- settled behavior and limits

## Actions

1. Add one report-only helper for `${TMPDIR:-/tmp}`, `~/.cache` excluding known tool caches, runtime scratch roots, and registered worktree `.tmp/` directories. Deduplicate overlapping roots, rank candidates by allocated bytes, and report unreadable paths separately.
2. Add optional structured history readers for Claude, Codex and Pi. Search only histories newer than candidate mtime; support absolute, `~` and `$HOME` spellings; exclude the currently running report session. Redact command excerpts and label mention, attempted, created and inferred evidence distinctly. Pi `--no-session` children remain unattributed.
3. Report candidate path/bytes, excerpt and source file/line when safe, session identity, liveness (`live`, `unknown`, `confirmed exited`), ticket-name hint, and references from PR bodies, verdict files or branch commits. Keep unattributed candidates visible. Roar scopes to current session and nested agents; lair scopes to the host.
4. Add a session-start warning for low free space on `/tmp` and `/home` without blocking startup.
5. Invoke the report from roar and lair, passing runtime and scope explicitly.

## Test

- First write positive-control tests for each history format, including a tilde-spelled candidate path, a nonexistent path, secret-bearing command redaction, a live creator, a cited candidate, and a Pi no-session/unattributed candidate.
- Verify scan deduplication, known-cache exclusion, unreadable-root reporting, allocated-byte ordering, and the startup warning threshold with temporary fixture roots.

## Invariants

- Reporting only: no delete, move, chmod, or cleanup operation.
- History hits are evidence of citation, not proof of creation; misses never prove no owner.
- Never emit raw credential-bearing history excerpts.
- No generic age- or name-based deletion, and no behavior change to existing WIP/liveness guards.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Roar and lair produce the documented report with explicit runtime and scope.
- [ ] All supported readers pass positive controls and preserve uncertainty labels.
- [ ] Startup healthcheck warns for low `/tmp` and `/home` space without blocking.
- [ ] Targeted tests and the declared repository check pass.
- [ ] Ticket 1118 closes in its own reviewed PR; tracker 1095 remains open until the full child union is integrated and reviewed.
